<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Italian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was the unified Italian state proclaimed in 1861 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, lasting until the republic was established in 1946. It built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> through colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. The name Italian is also used across the site for Italy, its peoples and its earlier city-states, which appear in many other empire profiles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Italy" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
